<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53477" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάρτᾰ</span></b>  (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κράτος</span>), Adv., freq. in 
			Ion.
		 and Trag., rare in Com. and 
			Att.
		 Prose (v. infr.):—with Adjs. and Advbs., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>very, extremely</i>; with Verbs,
				<i>very much</i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. κακῶς ῥιγῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hippon.
					16
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσθλοὺς κ. μαχητάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristeas Epic.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἀπὸ θερμέων Χωρέων</span>
			<i>very</i> hot, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.27
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. θεραπεύειν τινά</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετρίως</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.80
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. δεόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					8.59
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὀξύ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Acut.</u>
					58
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. πρευμενεῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					840
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἰδεῖν ὁμόπτερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					174
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ καὶ μακρὰ κ. ἐστίν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1218
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥς σου κ. νῦν μνείαν ἔχω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					328
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				222
			</span></i>, etc.; once in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηλοῦ κ. βραχέος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ti.</u>
					25d
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληρεῖς ἔχων κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				342
			</span></i> (troch.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>surely, in very deed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. δ᾽ ἔστ᾽ ἐγχώριος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					413
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. δ᾽ ὢν ἐπώνυμος</span>
			<i>true</i> to thy name, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				90
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				658
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. δ᾽ εἰμὶ τοῦ πατρός</span>
			<i>all</i> on the father's side, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				738
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. δ᾽ εἴσ᾽ ὅμαιμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					939
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				592
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1252
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				312
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1278
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺ δὲ κ. φείδῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Amips.
					22
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ κ</span>., used to increase the force
			of a previous statement, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἀνέκαθεν λαμπροί, ἀπὸ δὲ
					Ἀλκμέωνος . . καὶ κ. λαμπροί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.125
				</span></i>
			; esp. in dialogue, <i>yes, verily</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ γάρ τινες ναίουσι . . </span>; Answ. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ κ. . . </span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					65
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆρ᾽ ἄν τί μου δέξαιο . .
			</span>; Answ. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ κάρτα γ́</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					90
				</span></i>
			; once in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ κ. μέντἂν . . καθείλκετε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ach.</u>
					544
				</span></i>
			; in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> also, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				1.71
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.181
			</span></i>; esp. with a slightly iron. sense, <i>with a
			vengeance</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς ὂ δὴ καὶ τὸ κ. ἐπύθοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.191
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				3.104
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.52
			</span></i>.</div>
